post.description:
A celestial object: a system, star, planet, moon, asteroid belt, station, nebula, anomaly, black hole or marker (`baseType`). Objects nest: `parentId` is the object it sits inside, or null for the top level of the galaxy. Which parents a base type allows is fixed (a planet goes in a system or the galaxy; a moon in a planet). x, y, z are a position in the parent's frame: light-years in the galaxy (+Y is galactic north), system units (roughly AU) inside a system, and body radii around a planet. `explorable` makes systems open a system view and planets or moons an orbit view. `appearance` holds only overrides of the type and subtype defaults.

Example body:

```json
{
  "name": {
    "format": "plain",
    "source": "Gudrun System"
  },
  "summary": {
    "format": "markdown",
    "source": "Capital of the **Helican** sub-sector."
  },
  "baseType": "system",
  "explorable": true,
  "x": 12345.6,
  "y": -40,
  "z": 8820.1
}
```

A named set of top-level objects drawn as a colored outline: a sector, territory or faction. Its `groupTypeId` (a universe setting) decides which layer it belongs to and how groups nest: a Sub-sector's `parentGroupId` must be a Sector. An object is in at most one group of each type. Members are managed under /groups/{id}/members. `outlineColor` defaults to the group type's color.

Example body:

```json
{
  "name": {
    "format": "plain",
    "source": "Helican Sub-sector"
  },
  "groupTypeId": "019a5b3c-7d2e-7f00-8a1b-2c3d4e5f6a7b",
  "parentGroupId": null,
  "outlineColor": "#c8a24a"
}
```

A lasting place, such as a city, fortress or ruin. Where it is lives in its location (PUT /entities/{id}/location): on a planet or moon at a latitude and longitude, at an object, at a position in space, or at another place.

Example body:

```json
{
  "name": {
    "format": "plain",
    "source": "Hive Primus"
  },
  "summary": {
    "format": "plain",
    "source": "The largest hive city on Gudrun."
  }
}
```

Something that happened. `dateText` is free text in the universe's own date format (such as "240.M41"); `dateSort` is an optional number to order events by. It may have a location like a place, and characters relate to it with the `participant` relation.

Example body:

```json
{
  "name": {
    "format": "plain",
    "source": "Fall of Gudrun"
  },
  "dateText": "240.M41",
  "dateSort": 240.41,
  "categoryId": null
}
```

A person or being, shared by every map of the universe (characters belong to the universe, not to one map). Link a character to the events they took part in with the `participant` relation.

Example body:

```json
{
  "name": {
    "format": "plain",
    "source": "Gregor Eisenhorn"
  },
  "summary": {
    "format": "markdown",
    "source": "Inquisitor of the *Ordo Xenos*."
  }
}
```
